Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:27:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] tools: vision_batch_check covers production's paths
 (promotion, resumed image turns, all groups, the opt-in)

The first harness never ran on a GPU and missed what production does: an image request alone on the solo path that
is STOPped and continued in a slot (BGENI prompt+out), follow-up turns that resume a cached image conversation, two of
the four pipelined groups, and the STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS opt-in. Every check now has a reference that follows the same
read path, a text control of the same length (a mismatch is NO-GO only where the control matches), anchors outside
the regions (the new binary without the opt-in, the solo path, k5 in --text-ab), REUSED asserted per request, the
startup facts (regions line, INFO, expert caches, WARNING lines) and one GO / NO-GO / INCONCLUSIVE summary per mode
(exit 0 / 2 / 3). tools/vision_check_smoke.py runs it against a CPU-only fake engine (20 cases, 88 s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
