+The modes, in the order to run them.  An engine start takes about 97 s on the production config; the minutes below add
+the requests at TESTLOG #71's rates (about 120 tok/s alone, 50-85 tok/s per slot beside others, prompts at about
+2,500 tok/s) and about 10 s for the image encoder on the CPU.  They are estimates, not measurements (about 22 minutes in
+all, 26 with --vision-off-arms).
+  1. --text-ab OLD_EXE   3 engine starts, about 7 minutes (5 starts, about 11 minutes, with --vision-off-arms)
+  2. engine mode         3 engine starts, about 9 minutes, with --expect-from <1.'s --out JSON>
+  3. --negative-control  2 engine starts, about 6 minutes, with --expect-from <1.'s --out JSON>
+
+ENGINE MODE (the strong one).  The engine binary and a strata-<model>.json with a "vision" block, spoken to over its
+stdin/stdout protocol (GEN/GENI alone, BGEN/BGENI <slot> into a batch slot, STOP), as tools/batch_test.py does.  Every
+scenario has conversations of its own: a request can only continue a conversation's full tokens or one of its turn
+boundaries, so no request can take up what another scenario left behind.  Each request's RESUME and REUSED lines are
+kept and checked where a scenario expects one.  The slots are spread so that image slots and text slots decode in
+each of the 4 pipelined groups (slot g * 4 + t is row t of group g), several of them in one group's window.
+  process 1 "refs" (STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS=1): the references, every other slot idle
+    - first the fresh solo runs of the (iv) follow-ups (information only), with ckpt=0: no turn checkpoint, and the
+      session neither continued nor parked.  ckpt=0 still saves the root at a first turn boundary of 2048 tokens or
+      more (generate.cpp 13423-13431): ivc.follow's is ivc.turn1's assistant header, so a checkpoint of ivc.turn1's
+      prompt stays behind.  The next request, of another conversation, drops it (12525-12531).
+    - every text request alone (GEN); each image of (ii), (iii) and reset alone in a slot (BGENI, read from the start
+      as in the checks), then alone on the solo path (GENI)
+    - the (iv) and promotion scenarios step for step as process 2 runs them, without the text slots beside them
+  process 2 "checks" (STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS=1):
+    (i)   text slots in all four groups == their solo tokens while a long image prompt is admitted beside them and while
+          the image slot decodes (a text slot of its group shares its windows, and a text request is admitted beside it
+          too).  On the pipelined path the slots wait while a prompt is read (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP is not production's):
+          what changes under them is the table's main region, which the image's admission rebuilds
+    (ii)  the image request in that busy batch == the same request alone in a slot, and == alone on the solo path
+    (iii) two different images and a text slot in the same group's windows, each == its references.  A mix-up of the
+          two regions shows only where the text after the pictures sits apart, n - max(nx, ny) (generate.cpp
+          12082-12086): read from the encoder's files, a criterion of its own
+    reset a text request into image B's slot (its region back to the identity), picture B into image A's slot beside it
+          (one picture's region replaced by another's), and once that ends a text request into its slot: each == its
+          references
+    (iv)  resumed image conversations (production's hot path: a follow-up turn that reuses its history):
+          live: a text slot decodes, turn 1 is admitted beside it, and right after turn 1 ends, its follow-up (nothing
+                in between: it continues the live session, REUSED = turn 1's prompt)
+          RAM:  a turn 1 of 1024 tokens or more, exactly one text admission (it parks turn 1 in the conversation cache),
+                then the follow-up beside that text slot (restored from the cache: REUSED = turn 1's prompt, and the
+                engine log says 'conversation cache: restored <n> tokens')
+    promotion (production's main path): a long image request alone on the solo path (GENI) is STOPped after about
+          --promote-after tokens and goes on in a slot (BGENI <slot> <rest> with the prompt and every token so far):
+          once in the server's order (serve/server.py: the promoted request holds the control lines, so its continuation
+          is admitted first, then the text request that arrived, into another group) and once text first (its admission
+          parks the image's conversation; the continuation restores it while the text slot decodes).  The joined tokens
+          are compared over their common length (STOP is asynchronous: the solo leg ends at a window boundary).
+  process 3 "optin" (the same binary WITHOUT STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS): no regions line, no mrope_slots in INFO, an image
+          admission beside a text slot is refused, an image alone in a slot is admitted and a text admission beside it
+          is refused - the last release's behaviour.  And the anchors that do not read a slot region at all: image A
+          alone in a slot, each (iv) turn 1 alone in a slot, and each (iv) follow-up and promotion continuation on the
+          solo path (GENI / GEN alone, region 0), resumed from the same source as in the checks (the live session, the
+          conversation cache).
+  How the resumed and promoted checks decide.  Each (iv) follow-up and promotion is compared twice: with the same steps
+          alone in a slot (process 1) and with the same steps on the solo path (process 3).  The second catches a fault
+          that processes 1 and 2 share.  == its fresh solo run, or the request uninterrupted, is information only (a
+          fresh read and a resumed one may differ in late tokens, TESTLOG reuse5_nodraft).  Each has a text control: the
+          same steps with a text-only prompt as long.  An image mismatch is NO-GO only when its control matches; else it
+          is INCONCLUSIVE, a difference of the path itself and older than the regions.  A control that differs makes its
+          own criterion INCONCLUSIVE.  A promotion is decided only where both solo legs ended alike: the same tokens,
+          drafts accepted and drafts offered (DONE fields 1, 6 and 7).  Multi-row solo windows leave another numerical
+          state than slot windows (TESTLOG #59 (4)), so a continuation from legs that ended apart may differ without any
+          fault.  Same tokens still pass; a difference there is INCONCLUSIVE.
+--negative-control: processes 1 and 2, process 2 with STRATA_MROPE_REGION_SKIP=1 (the admission skips the region copy).
+          Every image comparison must FAIL and every text comparison pass: proof that the comparisons see a missing
+          copy.  The variable's designed WARNING line is no failure there.
+--text-ab OLD_EXE: the deciding comparison is OLD_EXE --vision against --exe --vision with STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS=1 (what
+          production would run), plus --exe --vision without it (the default path and the rollback).  --vision-off-arms
+          adds OLD_EXE and --exe without --vision; new-novision is compared with old-novision, and old-novision with
+          old-vision only for information (a difference between vision on and off would be older than the regions).
+          Every arm: each text request alone, a batch (text slots in every group, a long prompt read beside them, a late
+          admission), batch == solo; a slot's state back into the main session (a slot BSTOPped mid-reply, its rest on
+          the solo path with GEN and the prompt and every token, as the server goes solo; the next turn of the long slot
+          conversation, admitted into the slot that holds it: the only resumed text request decoding in a slot that any
+          mode decides on); with --vision the image requests alone (GENI; BGENI alone in a slot; a long one; the (iv)
+          RAM pattern - turn 1 alone in a slot, one text admission, the follow-up alone in a slot).  Every token and
+          REUSED == the old binary's; where a BSTOP took effect at another token than in the old binary's run, a
+          difference is INCONCLUSIVE.  The expert-cache slots, the experts resident and the WARNING lines are compared
+          with the old binary's arm of the same --vision.
+
+GO / NO-GO: every mode ends with one summary, each criterion GO, NO-GO, INCONCLUSIVE or info, and exits 0 (GO), 2 (NO-GO)
+or 3 (INCONCLUSIVE); a usage error exits 64.  A text reply that ends too early to cover a scenario is INCONCLUSIVE, not
+NO-GO (a larger --text-max-new).  --out writes all of it as JSON: the criteria, every check, every request (its RESUME,
+REUSED, DONE, tokens and the engine log lines it caused), the pictures' grids and every run's startup facts.  The
+startup lines that decide GO, per run: the regions line, INFO, the expert-cache slots per GPU, the experts resident and
+any WARNING or unexpected ERR line (--allow-warning REGEX lets one through).  Engine mode compares the expert cache with
+the old binary's under the same flags (--expect-from, from --text-ab's --out); without it, with production's k5
+(CUDA0 6144, CUDA1 6656, CUDA2 6144, CUDA3 5632 slots, 100 % resident - measured with prefill borrowing, so a
+difference is only INCONCLUSIVE).  Each GPU's 'room for experts' line is kept beside them.
